# Bloodthirsty Conqueror, ruling 2024-11-08: "If you and an opponent both lose life simultaneously, and this causes your life
# total to become 0 or less, you'll lose the game before Bloodthirsty Conqueror's triggered ability can resolve." Bot1 starts
# at 1 life with the Conqueror and an Underground Sea; Bot2's Sunspine Lynx deals damage to each player equal to the
# nonbasic lands that player controls - 1 to Bot1 (Underground Sea) and 1 to Bot2 (Badlands) at once (CR 120.2). Bot1 is at 0
# and loses (CR 704.5a) before anything resolves, so Bot2 wins at 19 life. Control: with Bot1 at 2 life instead, the same
# damage leaves it alive (bloodthirsty-conqueror-simultaneous-loss-that-leaves-the-controller-alive-triggers). Caveat: the
# Lynx also stops life gain (CR 119.7), so this cannot tell "lost before the trigger resolved" from "trigger resolved and
# gained nothing"; no other card here makes two players lose life at once.

[Life]
Bot1: 1

